# C/C++ file block-header casing (local elaboration)

This is a **local** elaboration of shared **c-cpp-standards**. It is not yet in the upstream rulesbase.


## Rule

In C/C++ source and header files, **section block headers** (the labelled banner comments that divide a file — e.g. Synesis-style `/* ////…` / `* label` / `*/` blocks) must use **lowercase** labels, **except** when a word is an **acronym**.

* Prefer all-lowercase words: `includes`, `types`, `version`, `helpers`, `implementation`.
* Keep established acronyms in their conventional uppercase form: `API`, `REST`, `HTTP`, `JSON`, `XML`, `URL`, `UUID`, and similarly well-known initialisms.
* Do **not** use Title Case (`Includes`, `Types`) or ALL CAPS for ordinary words (`INCLUDES`).
* Multi-word labels stay lowercase except for acronym tokens: `public API`, `http helpers` → prefer `public API`, `HTTP helpers` when those acronyms appear.
* The trailing `end of file` marker remains lowercase (already conventional).


## Examples

```c
/* /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 * version
 */

/* /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 * includes
 */

/* /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 * types
 */

/* /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 * API
 */

/* ///////////////////////////// end of file //////////////////////////// */
```

```c
/* ❌ forbidden — Title Case for ordinary words */
/* /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 * Includes
 */

/* /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 * Types
 */
```


## Scope

* Applies to new and edited C/C++ files in this project.
* When touching an existing file’s block headers, normalise them to this rule unless the operator asks to leave legacy casing.
* When upstream **c-cpp-standards** absorbs this rule, this local file may be removed after sync.
